1
00:00:01,717 --> 00:00:04,064
(Q1) TC EMPLOYEE: Hi. Can I help you?

2
00:00:04,064 --> 00:00:09,931
VISITOR: I'd like to find out if you have any excursions suitable for families.

3
00:00:09,931 --> 00:00:11,068
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure.

4
00:00:11,068 --> 00:00:13,226
How about taking your family for a cruise?

5
00:00:13,226 --> 00:00:18,769
We have a steamship that takes passengers out several times a day - it's over 100 years old.

6
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:23,079
VISITOR: That sounds interesting. How long is the trip?

7
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:25,052
TC EMPLOYEE: About an hour and a half.

8
00:00:25,052 --> 00:00:27,490
[Q 1答案句： mountains 注意复数。  picture=photo] And don't forget to take pictures of the mountains.

9
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:30,786
They're all around you when you're on the boat and they look fantastic.

10
00:00:30,786 --> 00:00:36,145
(Q2) VISITOR: OK. And I assume there's a cafe or something on board?

11
00:00:36,145 --> 00:00:38,884
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure. How old are your children?

12
00:00:38,884 --> 00:00:43,202
VISITOR: Er, my daughter's fifteen and my son's seven.

13
00:00:43,202 --> 00:00:44,311
TC EMPLOYEE: Right.

14
00:00:44,311 --> 00:00:48,715
Well there are various things you can do once you've crossed the lake, to make a day of it.

15
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:52,644
One thing that's very popular is a visit to the Country Farm.

16
00:00:52,644 --> 00:00:58,225
[Q1-Q2之间跟定位词，feed the sheep] You're met off the boat by the farmer and he'll take you to the holding pens, where the sheep are kept.

17
00:00:58,225 --> 00:01:00,265
Children love feeding them!

18
00:01:00,265 --> 00:01:02,610
VISITOR: My son would love that.

19
00:01:02,610 --> 00:01:04,354
He really likes animals.

20
00:01:04,354 --> 00:01:10,162
[Q2答案句： horse，跟上定位句词 40 minutes，  on a] TC EMPLOYEE: Well, there's also a 40-minute trek round the farm on a horse, if he wants.

21
00:01:10,162 --> 00:01:12,233
(Q3) VISITOR: Do you think he'd manage it?

22
00:01:12,233 --> 00:01:14,744
He hasn't done that before.

23
00:01:14,744 --> 00:01:15,876
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure.

24
00:01:15,876 --> 00:01:17,928
It's suitable for complete beginners.

25
00:01:17,928 --> 00:01:19,739
VISITOR: Ah, good.

26
00:01:19,739 --> 00:01:26,840
TC EMPLOYEE: And again, visitors are welcome to explore the farm on their own, as long as they take care to close gates and so on.

27
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:34,059
[Q3答案句： garden(s).   along the side of  = by the ... 沿着……] There are some very beautiful gardens along the side of the lake which also belong to the farm - they'll be just at their best now.

28
00:01:34,059 --> 00:01:36,552
You could easily spend an hour or two there.

29
00:01:36,552 --> 00:01:37,959
(Q4) VISITOR: OK.

30
00:01:37,959 --> 00:01:39,981
Well that all sounds good.

31
00:01:39,981 --> 00:01:47,371
[Q4答案句： 疑似答案词， n出现， 先记下来。【答案前置-代词指代】 not included = at extra cost] And can we get lunch there?&nbsp; —TC EMPLOYEE: You can, and it's very good, though it's not included in the basic cost.

32
00:01:47,371 --> 00:01:49,134
You pay when you get there.

33
00:01:49,134 --> 00:01:50,618
VISITOR: Right.

34
00:01:50,618 --> 00:01:54,721
(Q5) VISITOR: So is there anything else to do over on that side of the lake?

35
00:01:54,721 --> 00:02:00,097
TC EMPLOYEE: Well, what you can do is take a bike over on the ship and then go on a cycling trip.

36
00:02:00,097 --> 00:02:08,211
There's a trail there called the Back Road -- you could easily spend three or four hours exploring it, and the scenery's wonderful.

37
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:13,313
[Q5答案句：map.] They'll give you a map when you get your ticket for the cruise - there's no extra charge.

38
00:02:13,313 --> 00:02:17,230
(Q6) VISITOR: What's the trail like in terms of difficulty?

39
00:02:17,230 --> 00:02:19,941
TC EMPLOYEE: Quite challenging in places.

40
00:02:19,941 --> 00:02:22,237
It wouldn't be suitable for your seven-year-old.

41
00:02:22,237 --> 00:02:25,809
[Q6答案句：experience] It needs someone who's got a bit more experience.

42
00:02:25,809 --> 00:02:35,806
(Q7) VISITOR: Hmm. Well, my daughter loves cycling and so do I, so maybe the two of us could go, and my wife and son could stay on the farm.

43
00:02:35,806 --> 00:02:38,385
That might work out quite well.

44
00:02:38,385 --> 00:02:44,619
But we don't have bikes here... is there somewhere we could rent them?

45
00:02:44,619 --> 00:02:47,833
TC EMPLOYEE: Yes, there's a place here in the city.

46
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:50,251
It's called Ratchesons.

47
00:02:50,251 --> 00:02:54,307
VISITOR: I'll just make a note of that - er, how do you spell it?

48
00:02:54,307 --> 00:03:01,364
[Q7答案句：纯听写。 字母] TC EMPLOYEE: R-A-T-C-H-E-S-O-N-S.

49
00:03:01,364 --> 00:03:03,931
It's just by the cruise ship terminal.

50
00:03:03,931 --> 00:03:05,579
VISITOR: OK.

51
00:03:05,579 --> 00:03:16,775
(Q8) [need 小标题分点，repair kit 原词， snack and some water = food and drink] TC EMPLOYEE: You'd also need to pick up a repair kit for the bike from there to take along with you, and you'd need to take along a snack and some water - it'd be best to get those in the city.

52
00:03:16,775 --> 00:03:19,289
VISITOR: Fine. That shouldn't be a problem.

53
00:03:19,289 --> 00:03:23,221
[Q8答案句： helmet， rent=hire] And I assume I can rent a helmet from the bike place?

54
00:03:23,221 --> 00:03:26,318
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure, you should definitely get that.

55
00:03:26,318 --> 00:03:36,875
(Q9) [Q9答案句： won't see any ... = there are no ...] It's a great ride, but you want to be well prepared because it's very remote - you won't see any shops round there, or anywhere to stay, so you need to get back in time for the last boat.

56
00:03:36,875 --> 00:03:38,226
VISITOR: Yeah.

57
00:03:38,226 --> 00:03:41,505
(Q10) [定位： price = cost] So what sort of prices are we looking at here?

58
00:03:41,505 --> 00:03:57,004
TC EMPLOYEE: Let's see, that'd be one adult and one child for the cruise with farm tour, that's $117, and an adult and a child for the cruise only so that's $214 dollars altogether.

59
00:03:57,004 --> 00:04:00,984
Oh, wait a minute, how old did you say your daughter was?

60
00:04:00,984 --> 00:04:02,443
VISITOR: Fifteen.

61
00:04:02,443 --> 00:04:14,901
[Q10答案句： $267.   干扰项4个 ⭐️⭐️] TC EMPLOYEE: Then I'm afraid it's $267 because she has to pay the adult fare, which is $75 instead of the child fare which is $22 - sorry about that.

62
00:04:14,901 --> 00:04:17,401
VISITOR: That's OK.

